1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,560
 What if I told you that you could copy and paste

2
00:00:02,560 --> 00:00:04,720
 a little piece of code onto your website

3
00:00:04,720 --> 00:00:06,380
 and potentially triple your revenue?

4
00:00:06,380 --> 00:00:07,220
 Let me show you.

5
00:00:07,220 --> 00:00:08,940
 It's called the meta pixel.

6
00:00:09,920 --> 00:00:12,560
 If you don't have this on your website,

7
00:00:12,560 --> 00:00:15,440
 stop running ads and set it up now.

8
00:00:15,440 --> 00:00:16,280
 Here's why.

9
00:00:16,280 --> 00:00:18,520
 So when somebody clicks on your ad

10
00:00:18,520 --> 00:00:20,040
 and goes to your website,

11
00:00:20,040 --> 00:00:23,500
 Facebook can't see what's going on from that point.

12
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:24,560
 But why does that matter?

13
00:00:24,560 --> 00:00:28,380
 Well, if Facebook can't see whether you get the customer

14
00:00:28,380 --> 00:00:30,140
 or they just bounce off of your page,

15
00:00:30,140 --> 00:00:33,480
 then they can't tell if your ads are working or not.

16
00:00:33,480 --> 00:00:34,320
 And without that,

17
00:00:34,320 --> 00:00:37,440
 they can't find more people like your customers.

18
00:00:37,440 --> 00:00:40,440
 They're just going to keep finding people that are random

19
00:00:40,440 --> 00:00:42,080
 that might like your product.

20
00:00:42,080 --> 00:00:44,020
 But with this piece of code,

21
00:00:44,020 --> 00:00:45,900
 you're basically telling Facebook,

22
00:00:45,900 --> 00:00:47,580
 hey, that one was a good one.

23
00:00:47,580 --> 00:00:49,500
 Keep sending me more like that.

24
00:00:49,500 --> 00:00:51,980
 Set it up, pay somebody to help you set it up.

25
00:00:51,980 --> 00:00:53,680
 I don't care how you do it, just get it done.

26
00:00:53,680 --> 00:00:54,840
 It's really important.

27
00:00:54,840 --> 00:00:55,560
 Have fun.

